  "claims": [
    {
      "id": "claim_4f0c2927ddd24e87b425a898d8fcfe39",
      "statement": "yolo is a single binary: the default command builds the core dependency stack, starts the core HTTP server in-process on an ephemeral localhost port (127.0.0.1:0), and then runs the bubbletea v2 TUI, which talks to that server only through the wire contract; yolo serve runs the server alone, with no TUI.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/yolo/main.go#L129-L256",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:669ce7197d3cf4a84d5ce38e01c64107a2b6b05223220f97826fc7a882453614:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_5a4c1599f0444be89c89f4c54cb549a9",
      "statement": "Process exit drains the engine (stops active turns), shuts down the listener, and closes the logger within a 5 s budget; a second signal force-kills instead of waiting out the budget.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/yolo/main.go#L268-L293",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:39001ec0eb37a99a2a021cd0a76e3dc4f945a07b5a5c938c8ad41aa54f8800b8:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_f0c3da11b38f4c859a4eda0eddb65024",
      "statement": "buildDeps assembles the core stack (XDG dirs, logger, storage DB at <data>/storage/yolo.db, event bus, permission service, profile-pinned config loader, provider registry, session engine); YOLO_LLM=fake with YOLO_FAKE_SCRIPT installs a static catalog plus the scripted fake driver so the test suite never hits the network, while any other env builds the live registry; a broken home is a startup error, not a per-request failure.",
      "evidence": [
        {
          "resource": "repo://cmd/yolo/deps.go#L28-L136",
          "version": "repo-lines-v1:sha256:73291e801b47f4dd58f369f6e7ee9578cf7fc048482933c6d8b9a0d950e990ca:"
        }
      ]
    },
    {
      "id": "claim_4b85f5aba77145579a7e8ca116f67bd2",
      "statement": "Package dependency direction is bottom-up: protocol (wire DTOs, single source of truth) is consumed by server, which is consumed by session, which uses llm/provider/tool/permission/config/auth/storage/bus with glob and log as supporting packages.",
